{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "יששכר חמר גרם", :translit "yissakhar hamor garem", :gloss "Issachar a strong-boned donkey"} {:he "חמור גורם", :translit "hamor gorem", :gloss "a donkey causes"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Qere reads חמור גורם instead of ketiv חמר גרם; Ba'al HaTurim links this to Leah hearing the donkey's cry"}], :frame {:text "Genesis 30:16 records that Leah came out to meet Jacob. The midrashic tradition explains that Leah heard Jacob's donkey braying, which prompted her to go out to meet him, and she then brought him to her tent (Genesis Rabbah 73:5). The conception that resulted was Issachar. The Ba'al HaTurim connects this backstory to the qere reading of חמור גורם in Genesis 49:14.", :sources ["Genesis 30:16" "Genesis Rabbah 73:5"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בין המשפתים", :translit "bein ha-mishpetim", :gloss "between the saddlebags"} {:he "למה ישבת בין המשפתים", :translit "lamah yashavta bein ha-mishpetim", :gloss "why do you sit between the saddlebags"} {:he "רובץ בין המשפתים", :translit "roveitz bein ha-mishpetim", :gloss "crouching between the saddlebags"} {:he "ואחסנתיה בין תחומיא", :translit "ve-achsanetei bein tachumei", :gloss "and I settled him between the borders"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["רובץ בין המשפתים" "למה ישבת בין המשפתים"]}], :frame {:text "The tribe of Issachar is identified with Torah study: 1 Chronicles 12:33 states that the sons of Issachar had understanding of the times, and the Targum renders it that they were all great masters of Torah. The Mishnah in Sanhedrin 11:2 describes the Chamber of Hewn Stone (לשכת הגזית) as half in sacred space and half in profane space, where the Sanhedrin sat. Targum Onkelos on Numbers 34:11 uses the Aramaic root תחום for the border of the sea.", :sources ["1 Chronicles 12:33" "Mishnah Sanhedrin 11:2" "Targum Onkelos Numbers 34:11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Qere reads חמור גורם instead of ketiv חמר גרם; Ba'al HaTurim links t